				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				106,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(indexing): Implement ScanDirectory module for recursive file discovery\n\nIntroduces the `ScanDirectory` module to provide core filesystem traversal capabilities for the File Indexer service. This module serves as the entry point for discovering files within a project structure, balancing thoroughness with performance.\n\nKey functionality includes:\n- **Recursive Traversal**: Utilizes the `ignore` crate to walk directories recursively while automatically respecting `.gitignore` rules and hidden file configurations.\n- **File Filtering**: Implements robust filtering based on include/exclude patterns, file size limits, and access permissions to ensure only relevant, accessible files are processed.\n- **Performance & Concurrency**: Supports parallel scanning of multiple directories using `tokio` and semaphores to limit concurrency and prevent resource exhaustion during large scans.\n- **Safety & Security**: Prevents infinite recursion via depth limits, disables symbolic link following by default, and explicitly validates directory permissions before access.\n- **Utilities**: Includes `GetDefaultExcludePatterns` to skip common build artifacts (e.g., \"node_modules\", \"target\", \".git\") and `GetDirectoryStatistics` for gathering filesystem metrics without a full index.\n- **Index Maintenance**: Provides `ScanAndRemoveDeleted` to identify and purge stale file references from the existing index based on current filesystem state.",
			"SHA": "ffe7e02c0259ce2cea69c93e9288e69af5007c9f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
