				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(indexing): Implement ProcessContent module for file analysis\n\nIntroduces the `ProcessContent` module to provide foundational capabilities for analyzing raw file content within the File Indexer service. This module serves as a prerequisite for advanced parsing operations by handling the preliminary classification and sanitization of file data.\n\nKey functionality includes:\n- **Encoding Detection**: Identifies text encodings such as UTF-8, UTF-16 (BE/LE), UTF-32 (BE/LE), and ASCII by checking BOM markers and byte ranges.\n- **MIME Type Detection**: Determines file types using a comprehensive extension mapping (e.g., .rs, .ts, .py) and falls back to content-based detection using magic numbers (e.g., JSON shebangs, XML headers).\n- **Language Identification**: Resolves programming language strings (e.g., 'rust', 'typescript') from file extensions or shebang lines in executable scripts.\n- **Binary & Text Analysis**: Heuristically detects binary files using null byte frequency and byte ratios to prevent processing non-text assets.\n- **Tokenization**: Splits text content into lowercase alphanumeric tokens suitable for search indexing.\n- **Sanitization & Utilities**: Provides functions to strip null/control characters, count lines/chars, and safely convert byte arrays to UTF-8 strings.",
			"SHA": "4626b157daa92a7e56f62050b9abc793dec82040"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-02T02:46:53Z",
