				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				103,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(indexing): Implement ExtractSymbols module for unified parsing and utilities\n\nIntroduces a central module to orchestrate symbol extraction across multiple supported languages, building upon the recently implemented Rust and TypeScript parsers.\n\nThe `ExtractSymbols` function acts as a dispatcher, routing file content to the appropriate language-specific parser (Rust, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, Go) and aggregating the results into a unified list of `SymbolInfo` objects.\n\nKey additions include:\n- **Extraction Logic**: Async function `ExtractSymbols` that handles language detection and delegates to `ExtractRustSymbols`, `ExtractTypeScriptSymbols`, etc.\n- **Utilities**: A suite of helper functions for managing symbol collections, including `SortSymbolsByLine`, `GroupSymbolsByKind`, `FilterSymbolsByName`, and `GetSymbolStatistics`.\n- **Data Integrity**: Functions like `DeduplicateSymbols` and `MergeSymbolLists` to ensure clean datasets across multiple files.\n- **Search Support**: `CreateSymbolIndex` and `FindSymbolsMatching` to enable \"Go to Symbol\" and Outline View features.\n- **Documentation**: Comprehensive module documentation covering architecture, security (safe parsing), and performance (line-based parsing).",
			"SHA": "7ef3d1895840083d5050a2bd2f8dea6eb2717275"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-02T02:46:33Z",
